<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Mam kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1250 CE – 1525 CE (approx.) · capital Zaculeu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The highland Maya kingdom of the Mam people, ruled from the fortress city of Zaculeu near modern Huehuetenango until its siege by the Spanish in 1525.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mam-people">Mam</a> are among the oldest established peoples of western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala">Guatemala</a>, and Zaculeu had been occupied since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-classic-period">Early Classic</a>. In the Postclassic, from around 1250, it was the capital of a Mam kingdom that controlled much of the western highlands until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiche-people">K'iche'</a> expansion pushed the Mam back.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Zaculeu stood on a plateau protected by deep ravines, with temples, plazas and a ballcourt. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mam-people">Mam</a> kingdom was a rival and at times a tributary of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kiche-kingdom">K'iche' kingdom</a>. Its society was led by a hereditary lord and noble lineages, and its economy rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> farming and highland trade.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1525 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-de-alvarado">Gonzalo de Alvarado</a> besieged Zaculeu for several months, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mam-people">Mam</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaibil-balam">Kaibil Balam</a> surrendered when his people were starving. The site was later restored in the 1940s by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-fruit-company">United Fruit Company</a>. Mam remains a major Maya language.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1250 CE – 1525 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class=